Lila steps up to MARK, kneels, and takes his hand with her unburnt one. Her body goes still, and David hears rustling. A second Lila glides up next to the first, glancing at David and then adopting the same pose as the first Lila, except that her hand, burning, hovers over Lila and MARK’s hands. She freezes like the first, and then the other three Lilas come, one at a time, to kneel beside MARK.

