She spots the remains of her phone on the road.

“It’s not arson if the material is never actually on fire,” she says. “And no, I committed manslaughter and massive destruction of state protected land while in a fugue state triggered by the destruction and separation of the device that held my mind from the other aspects of my personhood.” She takes a step down onto the road.

“Don’t move!” A handful of other officers pour out of more cars down-highway. They train more weapons on her.

Lila says, “There are innocent people here watching you. Get them to safety.”

One of the newcomers starts to approach, but the first officer shouts, “Do not engage! Suspect is dangerous and highly mobile!”

