“You are threatening me with lethal force,” Lila says. She takes another step, which is greeted by more shouts about not moving. She can feel the remains of her mind reaching out to her like a plant unfurling toward the sun. “I am asking you to remove the risk of collateral damage. Do your sworn-ass duty.”

== Thrast <thrast-1>
He knew when the Game concluded that he and Lenn had made an exchange, so he expects to appear in some liminal realm between Veneth and the beast that would claim it. He does not expects to have a body when he arrives. It is not a body of flesh, because this realm does not render flesh for those who occupy it. Instead, he is presented with limbs and torso of living amber, glittering with their own internal light.

Other facets of his being are presented differently here as well. His Citizenship is a marble mantle hanging from his shoulders. His Command is a spear tipped with shining iron. And his premonition of the end plays out the corner of his vision, no matter where he directs his attention.

This place is nothing but a Bridge, and it is not even a bridge made of true material, just as the effects of his identity are no more than alternative presentations. But though it is not actually a bridge fashioned out of stone and mortar, it is a Bridge reaching out to many realms, who reach for it in turn. Truly a wondrous place, and sure to be an effective tool in the future.

At once, Thrast feels a door behind him close and one ahead begin to form. From the one behind, the one that leads from the atrocity he left Lenn within, he detects the Wayward Queen’s special attention. So she prevents that place from reaching the Bridge. For the best. The door ahead of him, across the width of the Bridge, is Veneth. He knows this as surely as he knows his own mind.

Standing between Thrast and his door home is the Queen.

Mere says, “You were banished from Veneth, and may not return.”

Thrast says, “I was bound to a child and forcibly expelled. I can and will return to my home.” He reaches out with his Extension for the door behind her.

She lifts the Gilded Sword’s tip to point at Thrast’s chest. She begins to speak, and the Paradigms rise to meet her words. “I am Mere, the Queen of Paths and Chief of Messengers, and by that authority I revoke—”

The Spear of Qastra punches through her gut.

